blurb = "Depicts the actor Ichikawa Danjuro IX as Kezori Kuemon, a smuggler captain from the kabuki play Koi Minato Hakata no Hitofushi (also known as Hakata Kojorō Nami Makura).

The play tells the story of a merchant who accidentally boards a smuggler ship while on a trip to see courtesan, and ends up forced to join the gang.

Danjuro is famous for originating an iconic pose, the [i]shiomi no mie[/i] (\"staring at the sea dramatic pose\") in this play.

The poem on the top right reads:

[i]White waves,
On a night boat
light blue
sails raised.
The sound of waves.[/i]

The \"white waves\" mentioned in the poem are a kabuki keyword that alludes to plays featuring bandits."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
